4,-0.58,2],[1.73,-0.33,2],[-2.68,-0.24,0],[-1.39,-1.3,0],[-3.22,-0.7,0],[3.02,-0.84,2],[-0.36,1.21,1],[-0.48,-0.34,0],[1.94,0.14,2],[-1.07,-1.44,0],[2.53,0.69,2],[2.36,0.49,2],[-0.97,1.21,1],[-0.02,0.79,1],[-0.17,0.74,1],[-2.46,0.13,0],[-1.37,1.84,1],[-2.6,-0.68,0],[1.37,0.73,2],[-0.85,-0.04,0],[0.95,1.32,1],[-0.04,-1.76,0],[-1.66,-0.82,0],[-0.57,1.34,1],[0.17,-0.45,2],[-1.39,1.0,1],[-0.94,-0.96,0],[-0.11,1.41,1]]},"takeaways":["Views, likes and comments rise together (Spearman ρ: views-likes 0.777, views-comments 0.769, likes-comments 0.857); likes and comments are the most tightly linked pair.","Reach and interaction rate are different things: views are weakly and negatively related to engagement rate (ρ = -0.058), so the most-viewed videos are not automatically the ones viewers react to most.","Pets & Animals has the highest median engagement rate (9.4%) and Shows the lowest (1.4%). Kruskal-Wallis p < 0.001 with a moderate effect size (ε² = 0.094).","From lower to higher group, median views are 32,579, 18,430, 192,492 and median engagement rate is 1.0%, 8.2%, 6.1%. The groups are not ordered the same way on reach and on rate here, so the names reflect the combined position of all four measures. Silhouette 0.347 means weak to moderate structure: groups overlap and the data looks more like a continuum than separate clusters.","Among categories making up at least 5% of the higher-engagement group, Autos & Vehicles is the most over-represented (7.2% of the group, 1.74x its share of all videos).","For creators: interaction rate and reach are separate wins in trending data. Judge a video against others in its own category, because category sets the baseline for a good engagement rate."],"caveats":["Historical trending data (Nov 2017 to Jun 2018), not a live feed. Clusters describe this dataset and are not predictions of future popularity.","Every video here trended, so it was already popular. Patterns may not hold for videos that never trended.","Views, likes and comments are cumulative at the last time a video appeared on the trending list, so older videos had longer to accumulate them.","Clusters are a convenient partition of a continuum, not natural species. See the silhouette score.","The four features overlap by construction: views, likes and comments are strongly correlated and engagement rate is computed from all three. Distances therefore mostly reflect overall scale plus interaction rate; this is the measure set the brief suggests."]}